            "relation": "INHERITED_FROM",
            "target_entity_instance": "ERA5",
            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "The emergence of global-scale data-driven models like GraphCast27 has accelerated the use of ML in weather prediction and broader climate science applications. Similar models, such as Pangu-Weather28, FourCastNet29, and Aurora30, have been released in recent years and claim to be more efficient and accurate than traditional numerical weather predictions. However, since these ML models (GraphCast, Pangu-Weather, FourCastNet, and Aurora) are primarily trained using reanalysis data sets derived from PBMs, such as ERA5, they function essentially as emulators31. Therefore, they have inevitably inherited the major weaknesses of PBMs in representing urban-scale dynamics, such as simplified micro-scale physics32, insufficient resolution to capture heterogeneity33, and limited real-world data for parameterizing localized processes34.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
