            "target_entity_type": "SourceComponent",
            "paragraph": "A common and necessary practice is to use regional and urban-resolving PBMs, such as coupled Weather Research and Forecast urban canopy model (WRF-UCM), to dynamically downscale global simulations into urban-resolving grids (typically < 1 km at hourly intervals), progressively bridging the spatial hierarchy from synoptic to urban scales. [From Figure 4 caption: Strengths and limitations of current contributions to urban weather and climate modeling from a large-scale physics-based models (PBMs); b urban-scale PBMs; and c urban-scale observations...Figure 4b details Urban-scale PBMs, listing 'WRF-UCM framework' under the 'Physically Coupled' category.]",
